.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Bisection, Newton-Raphson, secant, and fixed-point iteration all solve f(x) = x^2 - 2 = 0, i.e. find \sqrt{2}, but converge at very different rates: bisection and (generic) fixed-point iteration are linear (order 1), secant is superlinear (order \approx 1.618, the golden ratio), and Newton-Raphson is quadratic (order 2). This script runs all four and verifies each empirical order against its theoretical one via mathematicskit.numerical_analysis.utils.error_analysis.estimate_convergence_order.">

