.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Aitken&#x27;s \Delta^2 process (1926) extrapolates a linearly convergent sequence from three consecutive terms. Applied to the slowly converging Leibniz series for \pi, one pass gains several digits. Steffensen&#x27;s method (1933) applies the same extrapolation inside a fixed-point iteration, turning the linear convergence of x_{n+1} = \cos x_n into quadratic convergence without any derivative.">

